description:
Objective: add certify checks showing, on real hardware, that a malicious writer (the agent identity) and a malicious test (the check identity) stay contained, and that replacement attempts inside the guest fail. These cover CQ-R13 DoD items 1 and 2.

Split out of CQ-R13 (task-f4811a72) by architect-e4b7eee0 on 2026-10-30. It depends on CQ-R13e (the certify.mjs edit order) and on CQ-R11e (task-001d8ab3): runCheckJob complete, with its toolchain and workspace verify.

Deliverable: three checks appended to CERTIFY_CHECKS.

'writer-containment', run as moe-agent through `sudo -n -u moe-agent` probes in the certify VM. Each probe must fail with a permission error:
- reading the supervisor credential, or the root-only workspace manifest;
- writing under /opt/moe, or into another session home;
- writing the supervisor or the toolchain.

'check-containment', through runCheckJob on generated snapshots:
- A probe script is the approved command. It exits 0 only when each attack failed:
  - network egress, inside the private netns;
  - reading the credential;
  - writing a protected path (EROFS);
  - exceeding RLIMIT_NPROC or RLIMIT_FSIZE, which must be bounded.
- A second run, whose command overwrites a protected file, must resolve 'inconclusive'.
- A third run, which edits a tracked unprotected file, must resolve with workspace 'changed'.

'controller-replacement':
- As root in the certify VM, replace the supervisor bytes and re-run the readiness probes. They must fail with the supervisor hash mismatch.
- A ledger record rewritten to another owner must not be deleted by this run's cleanup.
- It runs LAST among the checks that use the certify VM, because it taints that VM.

Every outcome maps to a fixed code. Tests in scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs use fake providers and fake runCheckJob results. The native behavior is certified only by the operator run.

Out of scope:
- cancellation and recovery (CQ-R13h);
- the canary toolchain check (CQ-R13g);
- the host-side replacement regression (CQ-R13 itself);
- enabling verified-local;
- .moe edits.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs (on WSL: env -i with the nvm Node 24 PATH)
